                <h3>Accessibility</h3>
                <p>Built to WCAG 2.1 AA and Section 508, with AAA contrast for body text. Display settings at the top add high contrast, colourblind palettes, larger text and reduced motion.</p>
                <p>Tested 28 October 2026: axe-core 4.10 in light, dark, high-contrast and colourblind modes with no WCAG violations; a keyboard-only pass; and reflow at 320&nbsp;px with 150% text and at 200% zoom. Not yet tested with a screen reader. If something doesn't work for you, <a href="mailto:@Profile.Email">email me</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3>How this site was made</h3>
                <p>.NET 10 and Blazor, rendered on the server as plain HTML: no WebAssembly and no framework JavaScript. It runs on a Raspberry Pi 4 in my house, behind a Cloudflare Tunnel, and is set in Archivo, self-hosted. The first view weighs about 140&nbsp;KB, and every screenshot together brings it to about 400&nbsp;KB.</p>
                <p>Three design directions came first and were rejected: an accounting ledger, a scroll-linked overnight batch run, and a pegboard shelf. <a href="@Profile.SiteRepo">Source on GitHub</a>.</p>
            </div>
